\section{How it decides}{

For a ramp of width \eqn{w} centred at \eqn{c}, the level is \eqn{a}
before \eqn{c - w/2}, \eqn{b} after \eqn{c + w/2}, and linear between,
so for fixed \eqn{(c, w)} the fit is ordinary least squares in
